-- title:
--   Central scalars act trivially on the K(q)-invariants
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $g$ a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$, $q$ a prime, and $\Phi$ a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ which is an adelic lift of $g$ in the sense that: $\Phi(\gamma x) = \Phi(x)$ for all $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$ embedded diagonally and all $x$; $\Phi(x u) = \Phi(x)$ for every $u$ in the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, embedded into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ through the finite adeles; and $\Phi(h) = (g \mid[2] \, h_\infty)(i)$ whenever the finite part of $h$ is trivial and its real component $h_\infty$ lies in $\mathrm{GL}_2^{+}(\mathbb{R})$. Let $V$ be a complex vector space carrying a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-action commuting with the scalars, and let $f : V \to \mathrm{AdelicSpan}\,\Phi$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-linear map into the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$-translates of $\Phi$, which is $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant, injective, and whose range is exactly the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-orbit of the tautological vector $\Phi$ itself. Then for every unit $c$ of $\mathbb{Z}/q$, the representation [`LocalNewvector.gl2ReductionRep q V`](def/LocalNewvector_ReductionFunctor.html#L187) of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ on the subspace of vectors of $V$ fixed by the congruence subgroup [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup q 1`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181) sends the central scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ to the identity endomorphism.
--
--   This is the statement that the cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ have trivial nebentypus, read off at the place $q$: the centre of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$ acts trivially in the mod-$q$ reduction representation on the level-$q$ invariants of any realisation of the local representation generated by an adelic lift of $g$. It is used when identifying the type of that reduction representation for a newform, in the results that produce a representation of prescribed cuspidal type from inertial data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_IsAdelicLiftOf_gl2ReductionRep_scalarElem_eq_id_of_linearMap_range_eq_span.lean

